WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.750
- [Narrator] There's a
ramen shop on Rishiri Island

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.710
off the northern tip of Japan.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.850
To get there from Tokyo,
fly two hours to Sapporo.

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:09.730
From there, take the train to Wakkanai,

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:11.280
the northernmost city in Japan.

00:00:12.222 --> 00:00:15.240
You then catch a ferry to Rishiri Island.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.230
Make your way to the
western part of the island,

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.760
and once you're there
let's hope you're on time.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.350
It's only open two and a half hours a day.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.640
But the trip is worth it
because the place is said

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.283
to have some of the best
ramen in all of Japan.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:32.520
When it comes to ramen in Japan,

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.730
there are a few places
whose names will draw people

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.320
from all around the world.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.740
Ramen Miraku is one such place.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.360
And visitors come for this
special charred soy ramen

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.473
made with local kombu seaweed broth.

00:01:12.236 --> 00:01:13.540
- [Narrator] And this is no instant ramen.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.513
Making the dish takes hours.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.770
- [Narrator] The question, of course:

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.870
Why do you think people come all this way?

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:03.553
- [Narrator] Our turn.

00:02:03.553 --> 00:02:04.973
One charred ramen, please.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.282
(slurping)

00:02:09.282 --> 00:02:10.880
- [Narrator] Oh wow, this is good.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.498
(upbeat music)

